      "equations": [
        {
          "raw": "CLAIM ENTERS\n    │\n    ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  Q0  POSTURE CHECK                                          │\n│  \"Am I investigating or advocating?\"                        │\n│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n│  │ GATE: If posture = advocacy → flag bias, continue     │   │\n│  │ GATE: If posture = puzzlement → clean entry           │   │\n│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n│                                                             │\n│  FAILURE MODE: Confirmation bias. Motivated reasoning.      │\n│  Not a kill — but everything downstream is suspect.         │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n    │\n    ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  Q1  IDENTITY — \"What is it?\"                               │\n│                                                             │\n│  INVARIANT FUNCTION: Fix the object. Prevent identity drift.│\n│                                                             │\n│  PHYSICS VOCABULARY:                                        │\n│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n│  │ Entity types:                                         │   │\n│  │   axiom · law · hypothesis · theory · observation     │   │\n│  │   claim · mechanism · definition · equation           │   │\n│  │   evidence · operator · field · symmetry              │   │\n│  │   conservation_law                                    │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Axiom class: primitive | derived | boundary | disputed│   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Physics type:                                         │   │\n│  │   classical · quantum · relativistic · thermodynamic  │   │\n│  │   information_theoretic · consciousness · unified     │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Formalism:                                            │   │\n│  │   equation · inequality · operator · field_equation   │   │\n│  │   lagrangian · hamiltonian · lindblad · conservation  │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Master Equation variable:                             │   │\n│  │   G · M · E · S · T · K · R · Q · F · C · none       │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Symmetry pair:                                        │   │\n│  │   G↔T · M↔F · E↔C · S↔R · T↔K · none                │   │\n│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n│                                                             │\n│  FAILURE MODES AT Q1:                                       │\n│  • Category error — calling a hypothesis a law              │\n│  • Identity drift — the object shifts mid-analysis          │\n│  • Bundling — multiple claims disguised as one              │\n│  • Missing formalism — physics claim with no math           │\n│                                                             │\n│  PHYSICS EXAMPLE:                                           │\n│  \"χ-field mediates dark energy\"                             │\n│  → entity_type: hypothesis                                  │\n│  → physics_type: unified (cosmology + consciousness)        │\n│  → formalism: lagrangian                                    │\n│  → master_eq: C (coherence)                                 │\n│  → symmetry_pair: E↔C                                       │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n    │\n    ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  Q2  LOCATION — \"Where does it live?\"                       │\n│                                                             │\n│  INVARIANT FUNCTION: Fix the domain. Prevent context drift. │\n│                                                             │\n│  PHYSICS VOCABULARY:                                        │\n│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n│  │ Subdomains:                                           │   │\n│  │   mechanics · electromagnetism · thermodynamics       │   │\n│  │   quantum_mechanics · general_relativity · cosmology  │   │\n│  │   information_theory · consciousness_physics          │   │\n│  │   moral_physics · statistical_mechanics               │   │\n│  │   field_theory · particle_physics                     │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Scale:                                                │   │\n│  │   quantum · microscopic · mesoscopic · macroscopic    │   │\n│  │   cosmological · metaphysical · multi_scale           │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Regime:                                               │   │\n│  │   linear · nonlinear · perturbative                   │   │\n│  │   non_perturbative · equilibrium · non_equilibrium    │   │\n│  │   critical                                            │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Isomorphism status:                                   │   │\n│  │   ISO-CONFIRMED — same equations hold in both domains │   │\n│  │   ISO-PARALLEL  — qualitative match, math unmapped    │   │\n│  │   ISO-ANALOGY   — surface similarity, different guts  │   │\n│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n│                                                             │\n│  FAILURE MODES AT Q2:                                       │\n│  • Domain confusion — applying QM rules at macro scale      │\n│  • Scale mismatch — quantum claim tested with classical tool│\n│  • False isomorphism — claiming ISO-CONFIRMED when it's     │\n│    actually ISO-ANALOGY (metaphor dressed as math)          │\n│  • Missing cross-domain — claim touches theology but        │\n│    only classified under physics                            │\n│                                                             │\n│  PHYSICS EXAMPLE (continued):                               │\n│  → domain: physics, consciousness_physics                   │\n│  → subdomain: cosmology, field_theory                       │\n│  → scale: cosmological + quantum (multi_scale)              │\n│  → regime: nonlinear, non_perturbative                      │\n│  → ISO: ISO-PARALLEL (not yet confirmed)                    │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n    │\n    ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  Q3  ASSERTION — \"What exactly is being claimed?\"           │\n│                                                             │\n│  INVARIANT FUNCTION: Pin the claim precisely enough to kill.│\n│                                                             │\n│  PHYSICS VOCABULARY:                                        │\n│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n│  │ Claim types:                                          │   │\n│  │   descriptive    — \"X is like this\"                   │   │\n│  │   causal         — \"X causes Y\"                       │   │\n│  │   ontological    — \"X exists / is fundamental\"        │   │\n│  │   predictive     — \"if X then Y\"                      │   │\n│  │   mathematical   — \"X = f(Y,Z)\"                       │   │\n│  │   mechanistic    — \"X works by doing Y\"               │   │\n│  │   normative      — \"X ought to be\" (rare in physics)  │   │\n│  │   conservation   — \"X is conserved\"                   │   │\n│  │   symmetry_claim — \"X is invariant under Y\"           │   │\n│  │   boundary       — \"X applies at boundary Z\"          │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Precision levels:                                     │   │\n│  │   vague · basic · detailed · mathematical · precise   │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Certainty:                                            │   │\n│  │   proven · derived · well_supported · tentative       │   │\n│  │   speculative · unknown                               │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Physics-specific claim fields:                        │   │\n│  │   coherence_prediction: increases|decreases|maintains │   │\n│  │   entropy_relation: opposes|generates|neutral|coupled │   │\n│  │   grace_dependence: required|enhancing|independent    │   │\n│  │   consciousness_role: fundamental|emergent|observer   │   │\n│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n│                                                             │\n│  FAILURE MODES AT Q3:                                       │\n│  • Vague claim — too imprecise to falsify                   │\n│  • Scope creep — \"universal\" claim from local evidence      │\n│  • Moving target — claim changes when challenged            │\n│  • Unfalsifiable wrapping — \"X is true in a way you        │\n│    can't measure\" (metaphysics disguised as physics)        │\n│  • Negation failure — can't state what ¬(claim) looks like  │\n│                                                             │\n│  THE Q3 TEST: Can you write ¬(claim)? If you can't negate  │\n│  it, you haven't said anything.                             │\n│                                                             │\n│  PHYSICS EXAMPLE (continued):                               │\n│  Claim: \"A scalar χ-field with S_χ = ∫d⁴x√(-g)[...]       │\n│  accounts for observed dark energy evolution consistent     │\n│  with DESI DR2 4.2σ signal.\"                                │\n│  → claim_type: predictive + mathematical                    │\n│  → precision: mathematical (has Lagrangian)                 │\n│  → certainty: tentative (awaiting Euclid Oct 2026)          │\n│  → scope: universal (cosmological)                          │\n│  → ¬(claim): \"No scalar field with these parameters fits    │\n│    the DESI data better than ΛCDM.\"                         │\n│  → coherence_prediction: increases                          │\n│  → entropy_relation: opposes                                │\n│  → consciousness_role: fundamental                          │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n    │\n    ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  Q4  EVIDENCE — \"What supports this?\"                       │\n│                                                             │\n│  INVARIANT FUNCTION: Weigh evidence. Three channels.        │\n│  They multiply — zero in one kills the whole score.         │\n│                                                             │\n│  THE FORMULA:                                               │\n│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │  E_final = PS × CF                                    │   │\n│  │  CF = (0.5 + 0.5 × ED) × (0.5 + 0.5 × EC)           │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │  PS  = Phenomenon Strength (data quality, n-size)     │   │\n│  │  ED  = Explanatory Depth (mechanism, \"why\")           │   │\n│  │  EC  = Experiential Convergence (independent agree)   │   │\n│  │  CF  = Confidence Factor                              │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │  WHY-PENALTY: If ED < 0.3, apply:                     │   │\n│  │    E_penalized = E_final × (0.5 + ED)                 │   │\n│  │    \"Data without explanation gets cut.\"                │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n│                                                             │\n│  PHYSICS EVIDENCE TYPES:                                    │\n│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n│  │ empirical       — lab measurement, sensor data        │   │\n│  │ experimental    — controlled experiment with result   │   │\n│  │ observational   — telescope, accelerator, survey      │   │\n│  │ mathematical    — proof, derivation, consistency      │   │\n│  │ logical         — valid argument from premises        │   │\n│  │ computational   — simulation, numerical verification  │   │\n│  │ historical      — past observations, archival data    │   │\n│  │ inferential     — best explanation from indirect data │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Evidence tiers:                                       │   │\n│  │   Tier 1: Replicated, peer-reviewed, σ > 3            │   │\n│  │   Tier 2: Contested but published                     │   │\n│  │   Tier 3: Speculative, unreplicated, or analogical    │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Replication: replicated | partial | unreplicated      │   │\n│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n│                                                             │\n│  FAILURE MODES AT Q4:                                       │\n│  • Data fabrication — evidence doesn't exist                │\n│  • Cherry-picking — only favorable data reported            │\n│  • P-hacking — statistical manipulation                     │\n│  • Correlation ≠ causation — association without mechanism  │\n│  • Single-channel illusion — strong PS but ED = 0           │\n│    (lots of data, no explanation)                           │\n│  • Authority substitution — \"Einstein said so\" ≠ evidence  │\n│  • Replication failure — can't reproduce results            │\n│  • Scale mismatch — evidence at wrong scale for claim       │\n│                                                             │\n│  PHYSICS EXAMPLE (continued):                               │\n│  PS = 0.75 — DESI DR2 4.2σ + Planck + DES5Y                │\n│  ED = 0.70 — Full Lagrangian, ghost-free, but coupling κ   │\n│              not derived from first principles               │\n│  EC = 0.65 — Multiple independent surveys agree on w(z)     │\n│              evolution, but no direct χ-field detection      │\n│  CF = (0.5 + 0.5×0.70) × (0.5 + 0.5×0.65) = 0.85 × 0.825│\n│  CF = 0.701                                                 │\n│  E_final = 0.75 × 0.701 = 0.526                            │\n│  Why-penalty: NOT active (ED > 0.3)                         │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n    │\n    ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  Q5  DEPENDENCIES — \"What must already be true?\"            │\n│                                                             │\n│  INVARIANT FUNCTION: Expose hidden assumptions.             │\n│  Find the load-bearing structure beneath the claim.         │\n│                                                             │\n│  DEPENDENCY TYPES IN PHYSICS:                               │\n│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n│  │ Axiom dependencies:                                   │   │\n│  │   \"Which axioms does this claim stand on?\"            │   │\n│  │   → A1.1 Existence, A1.3 Information Primacy, etc.   │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Law dependencies:                                     │   │\n│  │   \"Which laws must hold for this to work?\"            │   │\n│  │   → L01–L10 (Ten Laws of Theophysics)                 │   │\n│  │   → Conservation of energy, 2nd law of thermo, etc.   │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Theory dependencies:                                  │   │\n│  │   \"Which theories does this inherit?\"                 │   │\n│  │   → GR, QFT, Shannon information theory, etc.         │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Assumptions (usually hidden):                         │   │\n│  │   → \"Spacetime is continuous\" (maybe not)             │   │\n│  │   → \"Classical logic holds\" (maybe not at quantum)    │   │\n│  │   → \"Constants are constant\" (maybe evolving)         │   │\n│  │   → \"Independence\" (samples may not be independent)   │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Boundary conditions:                                  │   │\n│  │   → Initial conditions of the universe                │   │\n│  │   → Specific parameter ranges                         │   │\n│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n│                                                             │\n│  FAILURE MODES AT Q5:                                       │\n│  • Hidden assumption — claim depends on something           │\n│    nobody stated (most common Q5 failure)                   │\n│  • Circular dependency — A depends on B depends on A        │\n│  • Orphan claim — no grounding at all, floating             │\n│  • False floor — apparent grounding is itself unproven      │\n│  • Parameter tuning — claim \"works\" only for specific       │\n│    fine-tuned values with no explanation for why             │\n│                                                             │\n│  THE Q5 TEST: Chase the dependency chain all the way down.  │\n│  Does it terminate at a genuine axiom, or does it loop      │\n│  or float?                                                  │\n│                                                             │\n│  PHYSICS EXAMPLE (continued):                               │\n│  Dependencies:                                              │\n│  → Axioms: A1.1 (Existence), A1.3 (Information Primacy)    │\n│  → Laws: L06 (K = Information → Logos), L10 (C = Coherence)│\n│  → Theories: GR (Einstein field equations), QFT (ghost      │\n│    freedom), Shannon (entropy bounds)                        │\n│  → Hidden assumptions:                                      │\n│    ⚠ \"χ couples minimally to matter\" — assumed, not derived │\n│    ⚠ \"10 DOF multi-component ghost freedom\" — not proven    │\n│    ⚠ \"m_χ ~ H₀ ~ 10⁻³³ eV\" — estimated, not derived       │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n    │\n    ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  Q6  CONSEQUENCES — \"If true, what follows?\"                │\n│                                                             │\n│  INVARIANT FUNCTION: Map downstream. Generate predictions.  │\n│  Separate confirmed from untested from failed.              │\n│                                                             │\n│  PREDICTION TYPES IN PHYSICS:                               │\n│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n│  │ Confirmed predictions:                                │   │\n│  │   \"These already came true\"                           │   │\n│  │   (strongest evidence for a claim)                    │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Untested predictions:                                 │   │\n│  │   \"These can be tested but haven't been yet\"          │   │\n│  │   (future experiments, upcoming surveys)              │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Decisive predictions:                                 │   │\n│  │   \"This ONE test settles it\"                          │   │\n│  │   (the prediction that kills or crowns the claim)     │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Failed predictions:                                   │   │\n│  │   \"These were wrong\"                                  │   │\n│  │   (must be honestly reported)                         │   │\n│  │                                                       │   │\n│  │ Theoretical implications:                             │   │\n│  │   \"If this claim is true, these other things change\"  │   │\n│  │   (ripple effects through the framework)              │   │\n│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n│                                                             │\n│  FAILURE MODES AT Q6:                                       │\n│  • No predictions — claim has no testable consequences      │\n│  • Post-hoc rationalization — \"prediction\" made after data  │\n│  • Unfalsifiable consequences — predictions that can't fail │\n│  • Prediction inflation — trivially true predictions counted│\n│  • Missing decisive test — no single experiment that settles│\n│                                                             │\n│  PHYSICS EXAMPLE (continued):                               │\n│  Confirmed:                                                 │\n│  → DESI DR2: w(z) evolution matches χ-field prediction      │\n│  → Dark energy density compatible with m_χ ~ H₀             │\n│  Untested:                                                  │\n│  → Euclid fσ₈(z): growth rate suppression at z ~ 0.5–1.5   │\n│  → Galaxy rotation curves: χ-field modification predictions │\n│  → Propagation speed: dispersion relation at nonlinear      │\n│  Decisive:                                                  │\n│  → **Euclid October 2026**: fσ₈ measurement either          │\n│    confirms or kills the specific χ-field coupling           │\n│  Failed: none yet                                           │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n    │\n    ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  Q7  FALSIFICATION — \"How does this die?\"                   │\n│                                                             │\n│  INVARIANT FUNCTION: Name the kill conditions.              │\n│  Every claim carries its own death warrant.                 │\n│                                                             │\n│  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════     │\n│  THE FIVE UNIVERSAL DEATH TYPES                             │\n│  (same in every domain, every claim, every object)          │\n│  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════     │\n│                                                             │\n│  1. SELF-REFUTATION                                         │\n│     The claim destroys itself when applied to itself.       │\n│     Physics: \"All physical laws are observer-dependent\"     │\n│     → Then this law is observer-dependent → collapses       │\n│                                                             │\n│  2. INFINITE REGRESS                                        │\n│     The justification chain never terminates.               │\n│     Physics: \"Every force requires a mediating particle\"    │\n│     → What mediates the mediator? → infinite tower          │\n│                                                             │\n│  3. EMPIRICAL CONTRADICTION                                 │\n│     Observable reality says no.                             │\n│     Physics: \"Protons decay with τ < 10³⁴ years\"           │\n│     → Super-K hasn't seen one → claim dies                  │\n│                                                             │\n│  4. LOGICAL INCOHERENCE                                     │\n│     Internal contradiction — A and ¬A simultaneously.       │\n│     Physics: \"The wavefunction is both real and not real    │\n│     in the same sense\" → contradiction → dies               │\n│                                                             │\n│  5. EXPLANATORY FAILURE                                     │\n│     Cannot account for what it claims to explain.           │\n│     Physics: \"Dark matter explains rotation curves\" but     │\n│     can't predict the baryonic Tully-Fisher relation        │\n│     → partial explanatory failure                           │\n│                                                             │\n│  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════     │\n│  PHYSICS-SPECIFIC KILL CONDITIONS                           │\n│  (domain layer on top of the five universals)               │\n│  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════     │\n│                                                             │\n│  • Ghost modes — field theory has negative-norm states      │\n│  • Unitarity violation — S-matrix not unitary               │\n│  • Causality violation — signals faster than light          │\n│  • Renormalization failure — infinities can't be absorbed   │\n│  • Fine-tuning — parameters require 10⁻¹²⁰ precision       │\n│  • Solar system constraints — violates Cassini bounds       │\n│  • BBN violation — changes primordial element abundances    │\n│  • CMB inconsistency — conflicts with Planck data           │\n│  • Dimensional mismatch — units don't work                  │\n│  • Energy condition violation — negative energy density      │\n│                                                             │\n│  FAILURE MODES AT Q7 (meta-failures):                       │\n│  • Missing death warrant — no kill conditions named         │\n│  • Unfalsifiable kills — conditions that can't be tested    │\n│  • Weak kills — conditions so unlikely they're meaningless  │\n│  • Immunized claim — every objection has a ready escape     │\n│                                                             │\n│  PHYSICS EXAMPLE (continued):                               │\n│  Kill conditions for χ-field:                               │\n│  K1: Ghost modes in multi-component sector → OPEN           │\n│      (10 DOF analysis not complete)                         │\n│  K2: Euclid fσ₈ outside predicted range → NOT YET TESTED   │\n│      (decisive: October 2026)                               │\n│  K3: Cassini bound violated (|ξ| > 10⁵) → SURVIVES         │\n│  K4: Galaxy rotation curves don't match → NOT COMPUTED      │\n│  K5: κ coupling constant derivable from GR alone → OPEN     │\n│      (would make χ-field red